  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. Both lotteries have outcomes with probabilities below 20%: Lottery A has a -3000 Euro outcome with 0.2% probability, and Lottery B has a -6000 Euro outcome with 0.1% probability. According to the decision reason, these small-probability outcomes receive a weighted probability increased by 10 percentage points (i.e., 0.2% becomes 10.2%, and 0.1% becomes 10.1%). The reason then evaluates each lottery based on the weighted expected value of these outcomes. For Lottery A: (-3000) * (0.102) = -306. For Lottery B: (-6000) * (0.101) = -606. The reason would prefer Lottery A because it has a more favorable (less negative) weighted outcome.",
