{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on small probability outcomes (less than 20%) and applies a probability weighting rule: increasing their weight by 10 percentage points. In this decision problem, Lottery A has a single outcome (-500 Euros) with 100% probability, so there are no outcomes with less than 20% probability. Lottery B has two outcomes: -1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability. Neither outcome has a probability below 20%, so no outcome qualifies for the increased weighting under the decision reason. Therefore, the modified weights would not alter the original probabilities for any outcome, and the decision reason would reduce to a standard expected value calculation using unmodified probabilities. The reason can technically be applied, but its defining feature (probability weighting for small probabilities) does not activate in this case. The relevant information is that no outcome has <20% probability, so no adjustment occurs.",
